{
  "area": "mexico-cozumel",
  "method": "Cozumel island: the Parque Nacional Arrecifes de Cozumel on the west and south coasts plus the north-end sites outside it (Barracuda, San Juan, Cantarel, Villa Blanca); the east side has no named site on any list read. Official list: the CONANP/INE Programa de Manejo del Parque Marino Nacional Arrecifes de Cozumel (SIMEC 30_libro_pm.pdf), whose zoning units name the reefs (El Islote, Punta Celarain, Maracaibo, Chunchaka'ab, Punta Sur, Colombia profundo and bajo; Paso del Cedral, La Francesa, Dalila, Palancar Cuevones, Jardines, La Herradura and Ladrillos; Paraíso, Dzul Ha, Las Palmas, Chankana'ab, Playa Corona, Tormentos, Yucab, Tunich, Cardona, San Francisco, Santa Rosa); it counts as one list. Operator lists, one each: Deep Blue Cozumel, Scuba Du, Dive Paradise, Blue Note Scuba, Agua Clara Diving, Maple Leaf Scuba, The Reef Dive Shop (Playa del Carmen, sells Cozumel boat trips), Dressel Divers, Scuba XOC, ScubaTony (whose site map gives the coordinates used here) and Cozumel Divers. Blue XT-Sea's reef-map page now serves spam, Aldora Divers and Liquid Blue publish no site list, and Scuba Mau names none, so none of those counted; the Reefs of Cozumel guidebook site was read for leads only. A site is counted when named on two independent lists and divable on recreational scuba; Palancar and Colombia sections are separate rows because the park programme and most operators name them separately, and a list naming only the umbrella ('Palancar Reef', 'Colombia reef') counted toward no section. Devil's Throat (to ~130 ft) and Maracaibo are counted as advanced recreational dives because operators sell them as such. Excluded: one-list names, park-only names no operator uses, and El Cielo (snorkel-only). Maple Leaf Scuba and The Reef Dive Shop print near-identical lists in the same order as the Reefs of Cozumel guidebook; they are counted as separate operators but add no name the other lists lack. Counted 2026-10-14.",
